-- title:
--   Galois descent for completed points: Tate's Proposition 11, Step 3
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $K$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_p \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ (written `PadicAlgCl p`) that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and let $R$ be a commutative ring equipped with an algebra structure over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ such that (`hR`) an element $x \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ lies in the image of the structure map $R \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ exactly when $x \in K$ and $\|x\| \le 1$, and such that (`hinj`) this structure map is injective; thus $R$ is a model of the valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_K$. Let $h \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $G$ be a [`PDivisibleGroup R p h`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199), that is, a family of commutative rings $G_v$ carrying cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebra structures, finite and free as $R$-modules with $\operatorname{rank}_R G_v = p^{vh}$, together with surjective coalgebra maps $G_{v+1} \to G_v$ whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. Write $\mathcal{O} =$ `integralClosure R (PadicAlgCl p)`. Let $x$ be a completed point of $G$ over $\mathcal{O}$, i.e. a family of points $x_i \in G(\mathcal{O}/p^i\mathcal{O})$ — elements of the direct limit over $v$ of the $\mathcal{O}/p^i\mathcal{O}$-points of the levels $G_v$ — compatible under the reduction maps $\mathcal{O}/p^{i+1}\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}/p^{i}\mathcal{O}$. Assume (`hx`) that for every $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ and every $R$-algebra automorphism $\sigma'$ of $\mathcal{O}$ whose values agree with $\sigma$ after inclusion into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$, one has $\sigma' \bullet x = x$. Then there is a unique completed point $x_0$ of $G$ over $R$ whose image under the map on completed points induced by the structure morphism $R \to \mathcal{O}$ equals $x$.
--
--   This is Step 3 of the proof of Proposition 11 in Tate's work on $p$-divisible groups, in the case of the base $\mathcal{O}_K$ for $K/\mathbb{Q}_p$ finite: a point of $G$ with values in the valuation ring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ that is invariant under the automorphisms over $K$ descends uniquely to an $\mathcal{O}_K$-valued point, the descent resting on the theorem of Ax–Sen–Tate rather than on a level-by-level computation of invariants. It is used in the Cartier duality part of the theory, in [`PDivisibleGroup.CartierDuality.cpoints_eq_zero_of_forall_pair_eq_one_of_forall_mem_range_iff`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.CartierDuality.cpoints_eq_zero_of_forall_pair_eq_one_of_forall_mem_range_iff).
